# ◈ /etc/portage/package.use/athanor-binpkgs
#
# Prebuilt packages were built with a specific USE combination (see each
# atom's optional use: annotation in packages.list upstream). If your local
# USE flags don't match a package's build-time USE, Portage will refuse to
# use the binary and fall back to source — which defeats the point.
#
# Mirror the upstream build flags here for anything you want as a binary.
# Example, matching the sample packages.list entry for neovim:

app-editors/neovim lua -python
